# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Line endings, decided once instead of per machine.
#
# Without this file, git on Windows checks files out as CRLF while the content
# in history is LF. Every tool that reads a file then sees a different byte
# sequence depending on who cloned it -- which breaks byte-level checks (the
# upstream project has an ASCII-only rule, and this repo keeps it) and produces
# diffs that show every line changed for no reason.
#
# `text=auto` lets git normalise on commit and check out per platform;
# the explicit `eol=lf` entries pin the files where a stray CR would be a bug
# rather than a preference.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* text=auto

*.rs    text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf

# Binary files: never touch them, never diff them, never try to merge them.
*.exe   binary
*.dll   binary
*.zip   binary
*.png   binary
